const T = [{"id":"01_name_fullname","category":"Part 1","topic":"Name","num":1,"title":"What is your full name?","examiner":"What is your full name?","student":"My full name is Jiang Jingjing. In Chinese, the family name always comes first, so Jiang is my surname and Jingjing is my given name.","audio_m":"","audio_f":""},{"id":"02_name_like","category":"Part 1","topic":"Name","num":2,"title":"Do you like your name?","examiner":"Do you like your name?","student":"Yes, I am quite fond of it. The character jing can mean something quiet and clear, and I feel it suits my personality, because I am a fairly calm and focused person. It has grown on me over the years.","audio_m":"","audio_f":""},{"id":"03_name_meaning","category":"Part 1","topic":"Name","num":3,"title":"Does your name have any special meaning?","examiner":"Does your name have any special meaning?","student":"It does, actually. My parents told me they picked jing because they hoped I would stay clear-minded and gentle, no matter what. In Chinese culture, parents often put a lot of thought into a name, so it carries their wishes for me.","audio_m":"","audio_f":""},{"id":"04_name_nickname","category":"Part 1","topic":"Name","num":4,"title":"What do your friends call you?","examiner":"What do your friends call you?","student":"Most of my close friends just call me Jingjing, or sometimes a shorter nickname. It feels warmer and more relaxed than my full name, which I only really use in formal situations.","audio_m":"","audio_f":""},{"id":"05_name_change","category":"Part 1","topic":"Name","num":5,"title":"Is it common to change names?","examiner":"Is it common for people to change their names in your country?","student":"Not really. In China a name is usually seen as a gift from your parents, so changing it is pretty rare. People might do it if the name is hard to pronounce or has an awkward meaning, but otherwise most of us just keep it for life.","audio_m":"","audio_f":""},{"id":"06_study_work","category":"Part 1","topic":"Study","num":6,"title":"Do you work or study?","examiner":"Do you work or are you a student?","student":"I am a full-time student. I am in my third year at university, majoring in Pharmacy, which is the study of how medicines work and how they are developed.","audio_m":"","audio_f":""},{"id":"07_study_major","category":"Part 1","topic":"Study","num":7,"title":"What is your major?","examiner":"What is your major?","student":"I study Pharmacy, but what I am really into is using artificial intelligence for drug design. In my spare time I teach myself how to use AI tools, like GPT, to screen genes and potential drug molecules. It basically combines biology with computer science.","audio_m":"","audio_f":""},{"id":"08_study_like","category":"Part 1","topic":"Study","num":8,"title":"Do you like your major?","examiner":"Do you like your major?","student":"I really love it. It feels great when an experiment finally works, or when an AI tool points me to a molecule that looks promising. What keeps me going is the big picture, because at the end of the day I really want to help make cancer drugs one day.","audio_m":"","audio_f":""},{"id":"09_study_why","category":"Part 1","topic":"Study","num":9,"title":"Why did you choose this major?","examiner":"Why did you choose this major?","student":"Honestly, it comes from a very personal motivation. I have always wanted to do something that actually helps people, and developing medicine felt like the most direct way to do that. The fact that I can now bring AI into it makes it even more exciting for me.","audio_m":"","audio_f":""},{"id":"10_study_dislike","category":"Part 1","topic":"Study","num":10,"title":"Anything you don't like?","examiner":"Is there anything you do not like about your studies?","student":"If I had to pick one thing, it would be how time-consuming lab work can be. Some experiments take hours and you cannot really leave halfway, so it eats into my free time. But I see it as part of the process, so I do not mind too much.","audio_m":"","audio_f":""},{"id":"11_hometown_where","category":"Part 1","topic":"Hometown","num":11,"title":"Where is your hometown?","examiner":"Where is your hometown?","student":"My hometown is in the south of China. It is a pleasant place with beautiful scenery, a comfortable climate, and lots of delicious local food.","audio_m":"","audio_f":""},{"id":"12_hometown_like","category":"Part 1","topic":"Hometown","num":12,"title":"Do you like your hometown?","examiner":"Do you like your hometown?","student":"Yes, I like it very much. The natural scenery is beautiful, the weather is usually comfortable, and people there are friendly. I also love the food, because there are many tasty local dishes.","audio_m":"","audio_f":""},{"id":"13_hometown_childhood","category":"Part 1","topic":"Hometown","num":13,"title":"What did you do with friends?","examiner":"What did you often do with your friends in your childhood?","student":"When I was little, my friends and I often played outside after school. Sometimes we walked around nearby parks, and sometimes we just talked and shared snacks. Looking back, those were simple but happy days.","audio_m":"","audio_f":""},{"id":"14_hometown_future","category":"Part 1","topic":"Hometown","num":14,"title":"Plans for next five years?","examiner":"Do you have any plans for the next five years?","student":"I do have a rough roadmap. Quite soon I will be going to Boston for an internship, and after that I hope to continue improving my research skills and prepare for further study. So the next few years are mainly about learning and gaining experience.","audio_m":"","audio_f":""},{"id":"15_hometown_age","category":"Part 1","topic":"Hometown","num":15,"title":"Enjoy being your age?","examiner":"Do you enjoy being the age you are now?","student":"Definitely. Being twenty is a great age, I think. I am old enough to make my own decisions and chase my goals, but I still have lots of energy and not too many heavy responsibilities yet.","audio_m":"","audio_f":""},{"id":"16_accom_where","category":"Part 1","topic":"Accommodation","num":16,"title":"Where do you live?","examiner":"Where do you live now?","student":"Right now I live in a student dormitory on campus, here in Nanchang. I share the room with three other girls, so there are four of us altogether.","audio_m":"","audio_f":""},{"id":"17_accom_howlong","category":"Part 1","topic":"Accommodation","num":17,"title":"How long have you lived there?","examiner":"How long have you lived there?","student":"I have been living in the same dorm for about three years, ever since I started university. I have grown quite attached to it, honestly.","audio_m":"","audio_f":""},{"id":"18_accom_like","category":"Part 1","topic":"Accommodation","num":18,"title":"Do you like where you live?","examiner":"Do you like the place where you live?","student":"On the whole, yes. The best part is the people, because my roommates and I get along really well, almost like a little family. It can get a bit cramped and noisy sometimes, but the sense of company makes up for it.","audio_m":"","audio_f":""},{"id":"19_accom_change","category":"Part 1","topic":"Accommodation","num":19,"title":"What would you change?","examiner":"What would you like to change about it?","student":"If I could change one thing, it would be the space. Four people in one room means storage is always tight, so I would love a slightly bigger room with more room for my books and painting supplies.","audio_m":"","audio_f":""},{"id":"20_accom_house","category":"Part 1","topic":"Accommodation","num":20,"title":"House or apartment?","examiner":"Do you prefer living in a house or an apartment?","student":"I think I would prefer an apartment, at least for now. They are usually more convenient and easier to maintain, especially in a city. Maybe later in life I would like a house with a small garden, but that is a long way off.","audio_m":"","audio_f":""},{"id":"21_science_like","category":"Part 1","topic":"Science","num":21,"title":"Do you like science?","examiner":"Do you like science?","student":"I really do, which probably is not a surprise given my major. The thing I love is working out how things actually work, from the human body to the way a drug acts inside a cell.","audio_m":"","audio_f":""},{"id":"22_science_school","category":"Part 1","topic":"Science","num":22,"title":"Did you learn science at school?","examiner":"Did you learn science at school?","student":"Yes, we did biology, chemistry and physics. To be honest I was not crazy about all of them, but I always had a soft spot for biology and chemistry, and that is pretty much what led me into pharmacy.","audio_m":"","audio_f":""},{"id":"23_cars_have","category":"Part 1","topic":"Cars","num":23,"title":"Do you have a car?","examiner":"Do you have a car?","student":"No, I do not. I am a student, so I mostly walk or take the bus, and honestly the campus is small enough that I do not really need one yet.","audio_m":"","audio_f":""},{"id":"24_cars_future","category":"Part 1","topic":"Cars","num":24,"title":"Want to buy a car?","examiner":"Do you want to buy a car in the future?","student":"Maybe one day, when I am working and settled down. The thing is, a car would be handy for getting around, but I am in no rush, because public transport works fine for me now.","audio_m":"","audio_f":""},{"id":"25_shopping_like","category":"Part 1","topic":"Shopping","num":25,"title":"Do you like shopping?","examiner":"Do you like shopping?","student":"It depends on what I am buying. I am not really one for clothes shopping, but I quite enjoy browsing for art supplies or little things for my dorm, because that actually feels relaxing.","audio_m":"","audio_f":""},{"id":"26_shopping_online","category":"Part 1","topic":"Shopping","num":26,"title":"Online or in stores?","examiner":"Do you prefer shopping online or in stores?","student":"Mostly online, to be honest. It is quick and I can compare prices easily. But for things like clothes or paint, I would rather go in person, since you can see the real colour and quality.","audio_m":"","audio_f":""},{"id":"27_watch_wear","category":"Part 1","topic":"Watch","num":27,"title":"Do you wear a watch?","examiner":"Do you wear a watch?","student":"Not very often, to be honest. I usually just check the time on my phone. I do have a simple watch, but I mainly wear it on days when I want to look a bit neater.","audio_m":"","audio_f":""},{"id":"28_watch_gift","category":"Part 1","topic":"Watch","num":28,"title":"Watch as a gift?","examiner":"Have you ever got a watch as a gift?","student":"Yes, my parents gave me one when I started university. It is nothing fancy, but it means a lot to me because it reminds me of home whenever I look at it.","audio_m":"","audio_f":""},{"id":"29_music_kind","category":"Part 1","topic":"Music","num":29,"title":"What music do you like?","examiner":"What kind of music do you like?","student":"I am really into piano pieces. I find them calm and kind of elegant, and they help me focus when I am studying or drawing. I am not really one for loud, fast music.","audio_m":"","audio_f":""},{"id":"30_music_change","category":"Part 1","topic":"Music","num":30,"title":"Has your taste changed?","examiner":"Has the music you like changed over time?","student":"A little, yes. When I was younger I just listened to whatever was popular, but as I have grown up my taste has got quieter, and now I lean towards instrumental stuff.","audio_m":"","audio_f":""},{"id":"31_social_media","category":"Part 1","topic":"Social Media","num":31,"title":"Do you use social media?","examiner":"Do you use social media?","student":"I do, but not as much as some people. I mainly use it to keep up with friends and to follow a few art and science accounts that I find interesting.","audio_m":"","audio_f":""},{"id":"32_social_media_time","category":"Part 1","topic":"Social Media","num":32,"title":"How much time on social media?","examiner":"How much time do you spend on social media?","student":"Probably less than an hour a day, to be honest. I try not to overdo it, because it can eat up your time without you even noticing.","audio_m":"","audio_f":""},{"id":"33_teachers_favourite","category":"Part 1","topic":"Teachers","num":33,"title":"Who was your favourite teacher?","examiner":"Who was your favourite teacher?","student":"Probably my chemistry teacher in high school. She had a way of making hard topics feel simple, and she was the one who first got me interested in how medicines work.","audio_m":"","audio_f":""},{"id":"34_teachers_touch","category":"Part 1","topic":"Teachers","num":34,"title":"Keep in touch with teachers?","examiner":"Do you still keep in touch with your teachers?","student":"With one or two, yes. I message my old chemistry teacher now and then, mostly to tell her how my studies are going, because she really shaped the path I am on.","audio_m":"","audio_f":""},{"id":"35_tidiness","category":"Part 1","topic":"Tidiness","num":35,"title":"Are you a tidy person?","examiner":"Are you a tidy person?","student":"I would say fairly tidy now, although it took me a while to get there. I like my desk clear when I am studying, because a messy space really distracts me.","audio_m":"","audio_f":""},{"id":"36_headphones","category":"Part 1","topic":"Headphones","num":36,"title":"Do you use headphones?","examiner":"Do you often use headphones?","student":"Pretty much every day. I use them for music while I study, and for video calls too. They help me block out noise, which is a lifesaver in a shared dorm.","audio_m":"","audio_f":""},{"id":"37_comedy","category":"Part 1","topic":"Comedy","num":37,"title":"Do you like comedies?","examiner":"Do you like watching comedies?","student":"I love them, actually. After a long day in the lab, a good comedy is exactly what I need to unwind. Laughing really does take my mind off everything.","audio_m":"","audio_f":""},{"id":"38_clothes","category":"Part 1","topic":"Clothes","num":38,"title":"What clothes do you wear?","examiner":"What kind of clothes do you usually wear?","student":"Pretty simple, comfortable things, to be honest. I am a fairly plain dresser, so I go for jeans and a jumper most days, especially when I am heading to the lab.","audio_m":"","audio_f":""},{"id":"39_parks","category":"Part 1","topic":"Parks","num":39,"title":"Do you go to parks?","examiner":"Do you often go to parks?","student":"Fairly often, yes, mostly to the lake near campus. I love going for a walk there when I need to clear my head after studying. It is my little escape from the books.","audio_m":"","audio_f":""},{"id":"40_art","category":"Part 1","topic":"Art","num":40,"title":"Do you like art?","examiner":"Do you like art?","student":"I love art, it is actually my main hobby. I have been drawing since I was a child, and painting is the way I relax and express myself when I am not studying.","audio_m":"","audio_f":""},{"id":"essay_A_pharmacy_ai","category":"Part 2","topic":"Long-term Goal","num":1,"title":"A: Pharmacy + AI","examiner":"Describe a long-term goal you would like to achieve.","student":"My biggest long-term goal is to do a PhD that combines AI with drug design, and one day help make new medicines for diseases like cancer. I am a third-year pharmacy student, and on the side I have been teaching myself how to use AI tools to screen genes and drug molecules. I have had this dream for two or three years now, ever since I realised the two fields could work together. It has slowly grown from a vague interest into something I am really set on. As for how I will get there, I am taking it step by step. Right now I am building a solid base in Pharmacy and learning AI on my own. And very soon I will be going to Boston for an internship, which I am really over the moon about. The reason it matters so much is personal. I really want to do something that helps people, and making medicine feels like the most direct way. I know it is a long road, but that is exactly why it excites me.","audio_m":"","audio_f":""},{"id":"essay_B_childhood_friend","category":"Part 2","topic":"Childhood Friend","num":2,"title":"B: Childhood Friend","examiner":"Describe a friend from your childhood.","student":"I would like to talk about a childhood friend of mine. We met in an art class when we were little, and we just clicked straight away, because we both had a soft spot for drawing. Back then we would sit together every weekend, painting whatever came into our heads, and showing each other what we had made. What I liked most about this friend was the sense of calm and encouragement. Even when my drawings looked messy, my friend would always find something nice to say, and that made me feel more confident. We are not as close as we used to be, because life has taken us in different directions, but I still remember that friendship warmly. It taught me that a good friend does not have to do anything dramatic. Sometimes just being supportive and sharing small interests is enough to make a friendship meaningful.","audio_m":"","audio_f":""},{"id":"essay_C_lab_team","category":"Part 2","topic":"Group Work","num":3,"title":"C: Lab + Teamwork","examiner":"Describe a time when you worked in a group.","student":"I would like to talk about a group project I did in the lab last semester. There were four of us, and we had to run a series of experiments and write it all up together. At the start it was a bit messy, but once we split the work and started to bounce ideas off each other, things went much faster. I was in charge of the data part, which suited me because I am into using AI tools to handle that kind of thing. It was not always smooth. Sometimes I had to get up early to catch up on the experiments, and once I messaged a teammate and waited ages for a reply, which was a little stressful. But when everyone pulled their weight, it just clicked and the work flowed. In the end we got a good result, and I was really happy. To be honest, working with others can be messy, but at the end of the day you learn a lot you cannot learn on your own.","audio_m":"","audio_f":""},{"id":"essay_D_hangzhou","category":"Part 2","topic":"Favourite City","num":4,"title":"D: Hangzhou + Scenery","examiner":"Describe your favourite city.","student":"My favourite city I have visited is Hangzhou, mainly because of the West Lake. The first time I went, I remember thinking it felt like stepping into an old Chinese painting. I love how calm it is. You can spend a whole afternoon just taking a long walk by the water, with the hills in the background, and it is the best way for me to relax. As someone who loves drawing, I found the scenery there really inspiring. I kept wanting to paint it. The city also has a nice mix of old and new. There are quiet temples and tea houses, but also modern parts, so it never feels boring. What stayed with me most was the slow, peaceful feeling. Where I study it is quite busy, so a place like that felt like a proper break. Every time I think about Hangzhou, I come back to that calm feeling, and honestly I would go again in a heartbeat.","audio_m":"","audio_f":""},{"id":"essay_F_coco_movie","category":"Part 2","topic":"Movie","num":6,"title":"F: Coco Movie","examiner":"Describe a movie you watched and enjoyed recently.","student":"I would like to talk about an animated film called Coco, which I watched a few weeks ago and really enjoyed. I saw it one Friday night in my dorm, curled up with my dorm-mates after a long, tiring week. We just wanted something light and warm to help us unwind. Without giving too much away, it is about a young boy who dreams of becoming a musician, even though his family is against it. He ends up on a colourful adventure where he learns the truth about his family past. It is funny and heart-warming, but it also made me a little teary by the end. The reason I enjoyed it so much was not just that it looks beautiful. Underneath the fun, there is a lovely message about family and following your dreams, which really struck a chord with me. After a stressful week, it was exactly what I needed. Honestly, the best films make you feel something, not just pass the time.","audio_m":"","audio_f":""},{"id":"essay_G_animal_book","category":"Part 2","topic":"Animal Story","num":7,"title":"G: Animal Picture Book","examiner":"Describe a story or book with animals in it.","student":"I would like to talk about a picture book I loved as a kid, which was full of animals. I cannot remember the exact title, but it was about a little rabbit who kept trying to find his way home. I must have read it dozens of times. What stuck with me was that the rabbit never gave up, even when he got lost again and again. As a child, that really taught me something about not giving up. Looking back, I think simple animal stories like that are great for kids, because the animals make big lessons easy to understand. Even now, in films like Coco, the friendly little dog is one of my favourite parts. So although it was just a children book, it left a real impression on me. To be honest, some of the simplest stories from childhood are the ones that stay with you the longest.","audio_m":"","audio_f":""}];
